dts: hubv3a: drop HS400, cap eMMC at 100MHz

The board booted but every write to eMMC failed:

  meson-gx-mmc ffe07000.emmc: 25 [0x260000], CRC[0x20100]
  blk_update_request: I/O error, dev mmcblk0, sector 2490368 op 0x1:(WRITE)
  EXT4-fs (mmcblk0p14): VFS: Can't find ext4 filesystem

CMD25 (WRITE_MULTIPLE_BLOCK) with status bit8 (TXD_ERR) set, i.e. a CRC
error on the data-out path. Reads were fine throughout - the read-only
erofs rootfs mounted cleanly - so this is the write path only.

meson-gx-mmc only tunes the read window (aml_sd_emmc_adjust_win /
emmc_ds_manual_sht produce "adj_win"/"tuning-c" in the log). The write
side gets a fixed delay from set_emmc_nwr_clks() and the log shows it
running with dly1 = 0, dly2 = 0 - no margin at all. scan_emmc_tx_win()
exists but is debug-only and never runs at probe. At HS400 400MHz that
was not enough for this part.

hubv3l uses the exact same node and does not show this, so it is a
board/part difference, not a software regression. HS200 at 100MHz is
plenty here: the rootfs is read-only and /dev/data sees little traffic.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-axg-thirdreality-hub-v3a.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-axg-thirdreality-hub-v3a.dts
@@ -530,8 +530,12 @@
 	cap-mmc-highspeed;
 	mmc-ddr-1_8v;
 	mmc-hs200-1_8v;
-	mmc-hs400-1_8v;
-	max-frequency = <200000000>;
+	/*
+	 * HS400 is left out on purpose: the driver tunes the read window but
+	 * never the write path, so writes ran without margin and every CMD25
+	 * came back TXD_ERR, which left mkfs unable to create data/overlay.
+	 */
+	max-frequency = <100000000>;
 	non-removable;
 	disable-wp;
 	init_core_phase = <3>;
